    "28": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Squad metrics",
          "heading": "Fiji concede 341 points across their last 11 international matches",
          "body": "Fiji have conceded 341 points across their last 11 matches, shipping an average of 31 points per game. During this same 11-match window, the Flying Fijians scored 331 points, averaging 30.1 points per fixture. The team's biggest win in this period came at home in September 2025, when they beat Canada 63-10 during the knockout stage of the Pacific Nations Cup."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV Global Series",
          "heading": "England respond to half-time deficit by crushing Australia in Salford",
          "body": "England secured a emphatic 48-15 victory over Australia in their WXV Global Series opener, recovering from an uncharacteristic 10-5 half-time deficit to extend their winning streak to 39 matches. Head coach John Mitchell praised the side's resilience, stating, \"It is an absolute joke if you are worried about being down 10-5. More important is how we worked our way back into it.\" The win, featuring eight tries, provides momentum ahead of next weekend's clash against Canada at Sandy Park."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "International Expansion",
          "heading": "World Rugby continues talks over staging Six Nations match in USA",
          "body": "Discussions persist regarding the potential to host a Six Nations match in the United States as part of a wider effort to grow the sport globally. While World Rugby has opened formal talks, the prospect remains a significant challenge. Reporting from earlier this week suggests that such a move faces hurdles, with skepticism from some involved unions regarding the feasibility of relocating traditional tournament fixtures. No official schedule changes have been confirmed as stakeholders continue to evaluate the commercial and logistical implications."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tournament planning",
          "heading": "The IRFU rules out moving Ireland Six Nations games to America",
          "body": "The IRFU has dismissed suggestions that it is considering relocating any Six Nations matches to the United States. Following comments from World Rugby chief executive Alan Gilpin, who suggested that an Ireland-Italy fixture could resonate with North American audiences, the Union issued a firm statement on Friday. The governing body confirmed there are \"currently no plans or discussions\" to move home games, maintaining that the opportunity for supporters to watch their teams on home soil remains central to the competition's appeal."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tournament expansion",
          "heading": "World Rugby continues talks over staging Six Nations match in USA",
          "body": "The proposal to host a Six Nations fixture in the United States remains an open topic. While World Rugby is actively pursuing the move as a means to grow the global game, recent coverage suggests that a deal is far from certain. Commentators have noted that securing the necessary union cooperation remains a significant hurdle, with many viewing the prospect as a long shot. No specific fixture or venue has been confirmed, and discussions between the governing body and stakeholders continue."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV opener",
          "heading": "Ruthless Canada hand Scotland heavy defeat in WXV series opening match",
          "body": "Scotland began their WXV campaign with a difficult 64-26 loss to a clinical Canada side in Edinburgh. Despite a spirited showing that saw Evie Gallagher and Shona Campbell cross for tries, the visitors ran in 10 scores to overpower the hosts. While interim head coach Dave Butcher had sought a seamless transition into the tournament, the scoreboard reflects the significant challenge Canada posed, leaving Scotland to regroup ahead of their next fixture against New Zealand at Hive Stadium."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Broadcast update",
          "heading": "Wales women to feature on BBC as WXV broadcasting plans confirmed",
          "body": "The Vodafone Wales WXV Series will be broadcast on BBC One Wales and iPlayer, the WRU has confirmed. Wales begin their home campaign against South Africa before hosting the USA, with the partnership aiming to extend the reach of the women’s game. WRU Chief Commercial Officer Tomos Grace noted that women’s rugby is the \"fastest growing part of the game,\" and this deal ensures top-quality international fixtures remain free-to-air for audiences across the nation throughout the autumn."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team History",
          "heading": "Argentina reflecting on their highest ever world ranking of No. 3",
          "body": "As the current squad looks to improve their standing in the Nations Championship, the team maintains a proud history on the international stage. Argentina reached their best world ranking of No. 3 during the 2007–08 window. Currently, Los Pumas hold an eighth-place position on the log after 3 fixtures, having secured 1 win to date. The side will look to build on their efforts as they continue the season’s competition."
        }
      ],
      "rung": "data"
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection conundrum",
          "heading": "Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii maintains open mindset regarding his long-term Wallabies position",
          "body": "Joseph-Aukuso Suaalii has rejected calls to specialise in a single role, confirming he is maintaining an \"open mindset\" to his positioning within the Wallabies backline. While the 23-year-old has primarily featured at centre, he insists he is comfortable covering fullback, wing, or the midfield. With head coach Les Kiss facing significant pressure to finalise his squad structure ahead of the 2027 home World Cup, Suaalii’s versatility remains a key talking point for supporters and selectors alike."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility dispute",
          "heading": "Naturalised League One players urge fairness regarding new nationality eligibility rules",
          "body": "The implementation of Japan Rugby League One’s new player eligibility categories remains a point of tension as the 2026-2027 season approaches. Recent reports indicate that naturalised players are actively lobbying for greater fairness within the system. While the league recently outlined updated criteria, the policy remains a contested issue among the playing cohort. Whether these concerns will lead to further amendments before the competition kicks off in December is currently unclear, as the league has provided no further official updates."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Rugby Asia 247"
      },
      "rung": "storyline"
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Series conclusion",
          "heading": "New Zealand fall to South Africa in final Test in Baltimore",
          "body": "The All Blacks have finished their series against South Africa following a 43-28 defeat in the fourth and final Test in Baltimore. Despite a late rally featuring tries from Luke Hanekom and Beauden Barrett, the visitors were unable to overcome a physical Springbok side that controlled the forward exchanges. The result marks the end of the four-match tour, with New Zealand now turning their attention toward the remainder of the international calendar as they regroup after a testing series."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-09-13",
      "edition": "Sunday 13 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Series victory",
          "heading": "South Africa defeat New Zealand 43-28 to secure series triumph",
          "body": "South Africa finished their four-Test tour on a high note, beating New Zealand 43-28 at M&T Bank Stadium in Baltimore on Saturday. The result marks a successful conclusion to the series for Rassie Erasmus’ side, who entered the fixture holding a 2-1 lead. Siya Kolisi praised the support following the win, stating, \"I want to thank every single South Africa here and back at home. We are so grateful. We do it for you each and every time.\""
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    }
